---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About - bneuhausz.dev"
  canonical="https://bneuhausz.dev/about"
>
  <div class="w-4/5 mx-auto py-10">
    <section
      class="flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-3xl border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-900/80 p-8 shadow-sm sm:p-10"
    >
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 lg:flex-row lg:items-center">
        <img
          src="/images/nb_face.jpg"
          alt="Bálint Neuhausz"
          class="h-32 w-32 rounded-full border-4 border-amber-100/20 object-cover"
        />
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div
            class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between"
          >
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-amber-200/70">
                About me
              </p>
              <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold text-amber-100">
                Bálint Neuhausz
              </h1>
              <p class="mt-1 text-base text-amber-200/70">
                Senior Software Engineer
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <a
                href="https://github.com/bneuhausz"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                aria-label="GitHub profile"
                class="group inline-flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-800 text-amber-100 transition hover:border-amber-100 hover:bg-amber-100 hover:text-amber-900"
              >
                <span
                  class="github-icon h-5 w-5 bg-amber-100 transition group-hover:bg-amber-900"
                ></span>
              </a>
              <a
                href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/b%C3%A1lint-neuhausz-61a4a4136"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                aria-label="LinkedIn profile"
                class="group inline-flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-800 text-amber-100 transition hover:border-amber-100 hover:bg-amber-100 hover:text-amber-900"
              >
                <span
                  class="linkedin-icon h-5 w-5 bg-amber-100 transition group-hover:bg-amber-900"
                ></span>
              </a>
              <a
                href="mailto:bneuhauszdev@gmail.com"
                aria-label="Send an email"
                class="inline-flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-800 text-lg text-amber-100 transition hover:border-amber-100 hover:bg-amber-100 hover:text-amber-900"
              >
                @
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-base leading-7 text-amber-50/90">
            Senior software engineer based in Pécs, Hungary, working with the
            same team since 2017. The company on my contract has changed a few
            times, but the work has stayed continuous: enterprise software,
            frontend modernization, and system integrations for industrial and
            business workflows.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-base leading-7 text-amber-50/90">
            I started as a junior and have owned technical and architecture
            decisions for most of my time here. These days I also mentor the
            developers joining the team.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.25fr_0.9fr]">
      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-900/70 p-8 shadow-sm"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-100">Experience</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
          <div
            class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
          >
            <div
              class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between"
            >
              <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
                IN2IT Business IT Solutions Kft.
              </h3>
              <span class="text-sm text-amber-200/70">Oct 2020 - present</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-amber-50/90">
              Subcontractor in the team formed from the old T-Systems group,
              primarily working on enterprise systems for TRI (Telekom
              Rendszerintegráció Zrt.), the successor to T-Systems Magyarország.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
          >
            <div
              class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between"
            >
              <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
                INNObyte Hungary
              </h3>
              <span class="text-sm text-amber-200/70">Apr 2020 - Sep 2020</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-amber-50/90">
              A technical employer change caused by restructuring at T-Systems,
              but the practical day-to-day stayed the same: same team, same
              office, and the same work context.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
          >
            <div
              class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between"
            >
              <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
                T-Systems Magyarország Zrt.
              </h3>
              <span class="text-sm text-amber-200/70">2017 - Mar 2020</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-amber-50/90">
              Started my career here after university and worked on enterprise
              applications in a team focused on internal software, warehouse
              workflows, factory systems, and integrations.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside class="space-y-6">
        <section
          class="rounded-3xl border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-900/70 p-8 shadow-sm"
        >
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-100">Education</h2>
          <div
            class="mt-4 rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
          >
            <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
              BSc in Computer Science Engineering
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-amber-200/70">University of Pécs, 2017</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section
          class="rounded-3xl border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-900/70 p-8 shadow-sm"
        >
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-100">What I work on</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-amber-50/90">
            <li>
              Warehouse management systems and factory software used in
              production environments.
            </li>
            <li>
              PWAs for handheld devices and forklift terminals used on the
              factory floor.
            </li>
            <li>Internal business applications.</li>
            <li>Internet-facing business web apps and workflows.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section
      class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-900/70 p-8 shadow-sm"
    >
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-100">Selected work</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
        <div
          class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
        >
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
            Warehouse management system
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-amber-50/90">
            A full warehouse management system for one of the country's largest
            beverage-distribution operations. It spans a management application
            for office staff and shift leaders, plus PWAs running on handheld
            scanners and forklift terminals for warehouse workers — all built in
            Angular — backed by an ASP.NET Core API and several .NET background
            services. I built the module that drives the warehouse's automated
            sorting line, communicating with its PLC over OPC UA, and worked
            across the background services handling scheduled jobs and client
            integrations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
        >
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
            High-traffic public web applications
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-amber-50/90">
            Public-facing web applications used by thousands of people daily,
            built and maintained as part of a long-running enterprise service.
            Distributed caching with Redis keeps them responsive under that
            load.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-100/15 bg-neutral-800/60 p-5"
        >
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-amber-100">
            System integrations
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-amber-50/90">
            Integrations between enterprise systems in .NET: SAP, message-based
            exchange over AMQP, REST and SOAP APIs, and file-based (CSV)
            interfaces with third-party software.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-amber-100/20 bg-neutral-900/70 p-8 shadow-sm"
    >
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:gap-8">
        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-amber-100">Stack and focus</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-amber-50/90">
            I led the adoption of Angular across our frontend applications, and
            frontend modernization has been a recurring theme in my work since.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-amber-50/90">
            Day to day I work full-stack: ASP.NET Core on the backend and
            Angular on the frontend, with occasional Node.js scripts and .NET
            background services in the mix, backed by PostgreSQL or SQL Server
            depending on the project.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-amber-50/90">
            Lately I've been learning and evaluating Flutter, as the need for
            native mobile functionality comes up more and more.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 lg:w-[22rem] lg:flex-none lg:justify-start"
        >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100"
            >Angular</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100"
            >ASP.NET Core</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100"
            >Node.js</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100"
            >PostgreSQL</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100"
            >SQL Server</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100 opacity-70"
            >Flutter</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100 opacity-70"
            >Redis</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100 opacity-70"
            >OPC UA</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100 opacity-70"
            >SAP</span
          >
          <span
            class="rounded-full border border-amber-100/20 bg-amber-100/10 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-amber-100 opacity-70"
            >AMQP</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
